      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T21:17:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I\u0027m thinking I\u0027m not a big fan of this. IIRC when using an input attachment you don\u0027t actually need a sampler at all. Instead you have an input attachment on the RenderPass and then you bind a DescSet with input attachment descriptor.\n\nThis makes me feel like if we need to use an input attachment then we should make that part of the RenderPassDesc. I\u0027m undecided now if we want to leave the presence of an InputAttachment on the RenderPassDesc to be enough to say we require a self-dependency or if we additionally want to pass another flag that says there is a self dependency on the RP.\n\nThe Texture and Sampler for DstCopy can stay paired together and renamed fDstTextureInfo if we want. This would be used for cases where we either have a copy (like today) or if we actually bind the dst as a normal Texture (e.g. desktop metal or gl).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 98,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "c471e4b4105cc602d96162f27bdf35668ef2f369",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f318f735_584c3127",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/CommandBuffer.h",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-22T03:00:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In another CL, I proposed having `dstCopyBounds` here and higher up in DrawList be used to hold the bounding box of pixels participating in any kind of dst read. With that approach, we don\u0027t need another parameter to addRenderPass here as the backend can check for it being empty or not when it implements the texture sample strategy.\n\nI do think it would be good to improve the representation capability in RenderPassDesc, but I don\u0027t want to require that to be a blocker for getting some level of input attachment / texture sampling dst reads working. It could be something that could go along with the eventual lifting of descriptor set / bind group management into the core graphite level.",
      "parentUuid": "601535ac_9fa8d8a0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 98,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "c471e4b4105cc602d96162f27bdf35668ef2f369",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15172bf9_63a68001",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/CommandBuffer.h",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-23T14:28:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we could get away without updating RenderPassDesc now. However, the higher level thing here is that input attachments have nothing to do with using Samplers. Right now we have no support (and no plans for it) for binding the dst as a texture with a sampler. We probably will want that for non arm macs and desktop GL if that ever happens (maybe d3d11 needs it??). But until we can ignore that.\n\nSo maybe its just a matter of renaming variables to not mention Samplers, but I guess my main point is that using input attachments is different.",
      "parentUuid": "f318f735_584c3127",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 98,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "c471e4b4105cc602d96162f27bdf35668ef2f369",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
